# tools/css/DRAFTS_COMMIT: a commit never changes, which the rendered pages at drafts.csswg.org do (the server renders the newest commit and its bytes differed from a
# pin a day old). Columns (tab separated): SHA-256 of the source, the file name it is kept under, its path in the repository. The fetch checks the commit and every
# hash and keeps nothing that differs; an existing copy is checked offline. Raising the pin is a deliberate edit of DRAFTS_COMMIT and this file in one commit that
# carries the re-read quotes (a quoted sentence is looked up in the source's plain text; see draft_text in the gate).
